    "titulo": "Supplier FAQs",
    "descricao": "1. How does a supplier do business with General Dynamics? 2. How can we get on General Dynamics' approved supplier list? 3. How does a small business contact General Dynamics? 5. What does General Dynamics look for in a supplier? 6. How do I find out which General Dynamics’ division is working on a specific contract? 7. Will our company have the opportunity to meet with a General Dynamics representative or be included in proposals and/or quoting process? 8. We currently do business with one business unit of General Dynamics. How can we get involved with other business units? 9. How does General Dynamics identify potential new partners for upcoming opportunities? 10. How can a supplier register as a potential source with General Dynamics? 11. If a supplier registers will they be certain to receive requests for quotes or purchase orders from General Dynamics? 12. Does a supplier have to register in order to do business with General Dynamics? 13. Once registered, is my supplier database profile visible throughout all General Dynamics business units? 14. How do I determine my company’s small business classification? NAICS codes, etc? 15. How can a supplier confirm their registration is complete?",
